# oracle: 27 TIP4P/2005 waters, pair lj/long/tip4p/long long long with kspace pppm/disp/tip4p (Coulomb and dispersion on the mesh, the O charge on its M site), pair_modify table 0 table/disp 0, NVE 50 steps
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 3.8e-12, atoms 2.6e-12. The O charge sits on its M site (pppm/disp/tip4p); the dispersion and erfc tables match the native default tables where the case uses them.
# oracle-inputs: w117cf_tip4p_pppm_water.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       w117cf_tip4p_pppm_water.data
pair_style      lj/long/tip4p/long long long 1 2 1 1 0.1546 8.5
pair_modify     table 0 table/disp 0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.1852 3.1589
pair_coeff      1 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.0 1.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 55.0 104.52
kspace_style    pppm/disp/tip4p 1.0e-5
kspace_modify   gewald 0.37833912 mesh 12 12 12 order 5 gewald/disp 0.3 mesh/disp 12 12 12 order/disp 5
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        1.0
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
